       "assumptions": [
        "Snapshot weighted least squares at each receiver epoch; no filter, propagation or coasting between fixes.",
        "Satellite positions are recorded IGS final orbits interpolated under the declared Lagrange policy; receiver positions are the scenario states rotated ECI to ECEF by GMST.",
        "One equal-variance measurement per usable satellite; satellite clock, ionosphere, troposphere and multipath are folded into the declared user-equivalent range error.",
        "Interference is a single aggregate receiver-plane SINR applied equally to every satellite.",
        "Degraded variance scales as 10^((nominal_min_sinr_db - sinr_db)/10), first-order code-tracking behaviour; illustrative until calibrated (GEN-273).",
        "Recovering and unavailable receivers produce no fix; reception resuming is not nominal accuracy.",
        "position_sigma_m is sqrt(trace(P_pos)/3), an isotropic per-axis ECEF value.",
        "geolocation_sigma_m is the navigation-induced horizontal error of a declared ground target located by pointing: the platform position error moves along the fixed line of sight onto the target's local horizontal plane, delta_t = (I - d n^T / n^T d) delta_r; sqrt((C_EE+C_NN)/2) of that covariance.",
        "Geolocation excludes attitude/pointing, time-tag, terrain-height and sensor errors; it is the navigation contribution only. A target below the minimum elevation has no geolocation."
